                <pb facs="0639" n="627" sameAs="frus:frus1940v05/pg627"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">832.24/255: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the Chargé in Brazil</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Burdett</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1940-11-02T17:00:00-05:00">November 2, 1940—5
                        p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>372. From the Ambassador. Your telegram No. 561, November 1, 3 p.m. Please tell
                    Aranha I spoke this afternoon on the subject in which he is interested to the
                    British Chargé d’Affaires here who promised to telegraph at once about the
                    matter to his government. [Caffery.]</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
